218: \footnotesize
219: 
220: \begin{columns}[T]
221: \begin{column}{0.48\textwidth}
222: \textbf{Operator Architecture \& Control Plane:}
223: \begin{itemize}
224:   \item \textbf{Custom Go Operator:} Built with Kubebuilder; extends Kubernetes self-healing directly into the network data plane.
225:   \item \textbf{Cluster-Scoped CRD:} Single declarative \texttt{NetworkRemediation} (\texttt{v1alpha1}) resource governing all monitoring and remediation.
226:   \item \textbf{Modular Subsystem Toggles:} Independent \texttt{enabled} flags for CNI, CoreDNS, and Pod Connectivity modules with zero coupling.
227:   \item \textbf{Three-Phase Pipeline:} Standardized \emph{Check $\to$ Evaluate $\to$ Remediate} reconciliation executed every 30\,s.
228: \end{itemize}
229: \end{column}
230: 
231: \begin{column}{0.48\textwidth}
232: \textbf{Core Capabilities \& Safety Guardrails:}
233: \begin{itemize}
234:   \item \textbf{$O(N)$ Ring Probing:} Adapted Pingmesh topology ($2N$ probes vs.\ $O(N^2)$ full mesh) with intra-node canary validation.
235:   \item \textbf{Configurable CRD Specs:} Users can define module specifications and detection thresholds directly in the CRD.
236:   \item \textbf{Safety Guardrails:} 30\,s cooldown windows, consecutive failure thresholds ($N \ge 3$), and bounded restart escalation.
237: \end{itemize}
238: \end{column}
